        "date": "2026-09-29T18:47:00Z"
      },
      "message": "Soften the mark: stroked path with round joins and round caps\n\nv3 was geometrically correct but every corner was a hard vertex - a needle\npoint at the centre of the M and sharp cuts where the diagonals met the cap.\n\nv4 draws the letterform as one stroked polyline with a single width, round\njoins at every corner and round caps at both ends. The centre vertex is now\nan arc, the shoulders are soft turns, and the stem ends are rounded. Weight\nstays uniform by construction, so the v2/v3 problem of diagonals reading\nthinner than stems cannot recur.\n\nThe site's nav mark is regenerated from the same geometry.",
